## Context

The accepted subject-matching decision groups different causes and separates reports of the
same cause. The #4471 executable views demonstrate the difference. Intake tags can disagree
with tenant-based classification, so they cannot determine the fix.

## Proposed replacement

Deduplicate exported rows by report ID. For each unique report, look up the tenant's locale
and booking form, then inspect its channel and body. Group duplicates by an evidenced shared
cause; keep uncertain reports visible with their source IDs and a request for missing facts.
An unknown tenant must stay unplaced until evidence supports a cause.

## Consequences and status

Triage takes more reading and tenant context. It preserves separate work for the shared
parser and booking-v3 hint, so one fix cannot close both by accident. Decision 0001 is not
edited. This replacement remains proposed until the support owner accepts it.

